# Discord Activity credentials. Two values, both from
# https://discord.com/developers/applications → your app.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then fill in the two blanks below
#
# You do NOT need this file to play Deep Field over Tailscale — the game runs
# without it. It is only read when the page is opened inside Discord.
#
# `.env` is gitignored explicitly (the `*.local` rule does NOT cover it, which
# is worth knowing before you trust it). Never put a real secret in THIS file:
# `.env.example` is the one that gets committed.


# ── 1. Your application id ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Portal: General Information → APPLICATION ID  (the same number shown as
# OAuth2 → CLIENT ID — they are one value).
#
# Public: Vite inlines this into the client bundle, where anyone can read it.
# That is how OAuth2 client ids work and is not a leak.
#
# IMPORTANT: this is read at BUILD time. `npm run build` and `npm run play`
# must be run with it already in place, or the Discord code is stripped from
# the bundle as dead code and the Activity silently cannot sign anyone in. The
# build prints a warning when it is missing.
VITE_DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=


# ── 2. Your client secret ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Portal: OAuth2 → CLIENT SECRET → Reset Secret (it is only shown once).
#
# Genuinely secret. Read by the relay to trade the Activity's one-time code for
# an access token; it never reaches the browser. If it ever appears in a client
# bundle or a commit, reset it in the portal immediately.
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=


# ── 3. Optional: a channel webhook for match reports ──────────────────────────
# Discord: channel → Edit Channel → Integrations → Webhooks → New Webhook →
# Copy Webhook URL.
#
# Set it and the relay posts one message per finished race — headline, sector,
# room, seed and both pilots' figures — so the channel becomes the match ledger.
# Leave it unset and no reports are sent, which is a perfectly good way to run.
#
# The relay sends these, not the browser. Inside a Discord Activity the page
# cannot reach discord.com at all, and one sender means one message rather than
# "configure this on exactly one machine or receive everything twice".
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=


# Optional: set only if your application id and the id the *server* should use
# ever need to differ. Left unset, the server uses VITE_DISCORD_CLIENT_ID.
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
